{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1470988-tc-assassins-why-daylight-twilight-shadow","id":1470988,"title":"[TC Assassins] Why Daylight/Twilight/Shadow?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-21T00:34:39-08:00","id":1470988,"title":"[TC Assassins] Why Daylight/Twilight/Shadow?","content":"Thinking about translating Lexicon of Assassins into Polish, I found some terms dissonance.<br /> <br /> <i>Daylight </i>and <i>Twilight</i> seems logical as to 'normal society' and 'criminal underworld'. Then <i> Shadow</i> for 'Assassins danger society' seems out of place - where Daylight and Twilight relate to day/night cycle - Shadow is the thing that shows only when Sun ( Daylight ) is putted on objects, behind them. Logical third term in this series would be 'Night', opposite of Daylight...<br /> <br /> <b>Are there some reasons why 'Shadow', not 'Night', was chosen as term for Assassins society?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-21-2021, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T01:10:21-08:00","id":1470989,"title":"","content":"That is actually quite a good question. Maybe, &quot;Shadow&quot; was used because there can be shadows in daytime while &quot;Night&quot; would be tied to a special time. Maybe, the authors thought, &quot;Shadow&quot; sounds cool....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24955-waldi","name":"Waldi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T03:19:00-08:00","id":1470994,"title":"","content":"Daylight is not day, it\u2019s the light of day, it would oppose shadow in that sense, as the light of the day is the most bright of them all.<br /> <br /> Twilight while can be translated as the time of the day the sun is setting, BUT it also means kind of Penumbra, something illuminated, but not completely.<br /> <br /> So, if you want to translate Shadow into something like night, it\u2019s better to translate Daylight into something like Bright Light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T04:17:33-08:00","id":1471000,"title":"","content":"Shadow can happen any time, anywhere. Its presence is always possible and ready to contrast current surroundings.<br /> <br /> Any time-related term just imposes limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T12:01:19-08:00","id":1471023,"title":"","content":"Technically, the same holds true of Daylight and Twilight. <br /> <br /> I'm not quarreling about the naming convention; I'm fine with it as it is. But I'd also be fine with it if it was \u201cDaylight/Twilight/Night\u201d or \u201cLight/Shade/Dark\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T03:29:55-08:00","id":1471269,"title":"","content":"<b>Why Daylight/Twilight/Shadow?</b><br /> <br /> My guess is because the cultural norms (in English/Western stories at least) - &quot;daylight&quot; is a wholesome light/time in which open, honest businessmen do their thing, &quot;twilight&quot; is a (literal &amp; metaphorically) shadier time in which you do things that must be hidden, and &quot;shadow&quot; is a term long associated with stealth, sneaking, and assassination.<br /> <br /> It's not a <i>direct definition </i>thing, but it is common thing in Western fiction. Day is good, Night is evil, Twilight is criminal (not evil, but not &quot;good&quot;), and Shadow is sneaky/mystical. Someone with a literature major could probably tell you why we settled on those associations and where they originate from, but they were probably chosen by Onyx Path because those associations are already well established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}